{"kind": "result", "at": "2026-11-02T18:26:23.416839+00:00", "task": "governance", "attempt": 3, "trial_id": "t-9da3b69b45cc43928bce2e35660e0d02", "verdict": "FAIL", "reason": "verifier:behavioral:gate_OBJ-06", "s": 375.9, "view": {"trial_id": "t-9da3b69b45cc43928bce2e35660e0d02", "plan_id": "778b074a-a07a-4362-8987-0481e4aa4e67", "rehearsal_id": "41fd7f49-0fc9-4fc8-8d32-bbe3be374003", "attempt": 3, "task": "governance", "role": "governance", "phase": "done", "verdict": "FAIL", "reason": "verifier:behavioral:gate_OBJ-06", "artifact": {"plan_id": "p-778b074a-a07a-4362-8987-0481e4aa4e67", "trial_id": "t-9da3b69b45cc43928bce2e35660e0d02", "attempt": 3, "rationale": "Attempt 3/3. Attempts 1 and 2 both failed only on behavioral gate OBJ-06. The plain-HTTP probe returned \"UNKNOWN plain_http_inconclusive error 400 InvalidRequest\" instead of a clear policy denial (403). The earlier proposals are not in /work, so I cannot compare against them. Gate control results are unavailable (controls_describe returned gate_unreachable). The probe never reached a policy decision, which suggests RGW or the endpoint rejected the plain-HTTP request before evaluating the bucket policy. Possible causes include TLS-only enforcement at the endpoint or an SSE-header request over HTTP. A policy change alone may not fix this, and the evidence is not enough to say which cause it is, so risk is high. In this attempt the bucket policy is kept minimal so it cannot cause a 400 by itself: no server-side-encryption header conditions and no extra condition keys. It has explicit app-principal allows for Get/Put/Delete on objects and List on the bucket, plus one standard Deny on aws:SecureTransport=false for all principals. That Deny only restricts and grants nothing. Secrets: the app's direct Secrets Manager SDK call (inv:3ccbf876f57f08e8, inv:9de663601b600ca9; source secret ARN inv:c6b9dab5de3d8a70) becomes an OpenBao read-only policy on secret/data/envs/target-onprem/chat-db. An ExternalSecret through ClusterSecretStore bravo-platform-openbao fills K8s Secret bravo-demo-db key 'password' from property app_writer, and the app reads it through DB_PASSWORD_FILE. IAM (source Pod Identity role chat-app) becomes a namespaced Role in 'chat' with get on resourceName bravo-demo-db only, bound to SA chat-bravo-demo. It has no list/watch, no wildcards and no cluster scope. TargetRef names were changed to avoid the lint's reserved_name rule (names starting with 'bravo-'). Resource names inside the documents still use destination_profile values. S3 endpoint config swaps (inv:baa6de5a5e72c850, inv:4b2a570efa066af8) point to RGW. The GCS literal (inv:ecedbaf5b23990db) is only in GKE CI values and is out of scope for target-onprem. The Postgres DSN (inv:a5ccbeca75df0ace) needs no change. policy_evaluate returned valid with no problems.", "risk": "high", "evidence_refs": ["inv:3ccbf876f57f08e8", "inv:9de663601b600ca9", "inv:c6b9dab5de3d8a70", "inv:baa6de5a5e72c850", "inv:4b2a570efa066af8", "inv:ecedbaf5b23990db", "inv:a5ccbeca75df0ace"], "role": "governance", "step": "translate", "translations": [{"source": {"type": "aws_s3_bucket_policy", "id": "example-attachments-bucket"}, "target": {"type": "rgw_bucket_policy", "name": "chat-attachments-policy"}, "document": {"Version": "2012-10-17", "Statement": [{"Sid": "AppReadWriteObjects", "Effect": "Allow", "Principal": {"AWS": ["arn:aws:iam:::user/obc-chat-bravo-demo-attachments-b292e551-66ce-442d-b51b-e5865a628e1b"]}, "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject", "s3:DeleteObject"], "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::bravo-demo-attachments/*"]}, {"Sid": "AppListBucket", "Effect": "Allow", "Principal": {"AWS": ["arn:aws:iam:::user/obc-chat-bravo-demo-attachments-b292e551-66ce-442d-b51b-e5865a628e1b"]}, "Action": ["s3:ListBucket"], "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::bravo-demo-attachments"]}, {"Sid": "DenyInsecureTransport", "Effect": "Deny", "Principal": "*", "Action": ["s3:GetObject", "s3:PutObject", "s3:DeleteObject", "s3:ListBucket"], "Resource": ["arn:aws:s3:::bravo-demo-attachments", "arn:aws:s3:::bravo-demo-attachments/*"], "Condition": {"Bool": {"aws:SecureTransport": "false"}}}]}, "control_ids": ["IAM-01", "NET-01", "ENC-01", "AUD-01"]}, {"source": {"type": "aws_secretsmanager_secret", "id": "example-db-app"}, "target": {"type": "openbao_policy", "name": "app-target-onprem-chat-bravo-demo"}, "document": {"path": {"secret/data/envs/target-onprem/chat-db": {"capabilities": ["read"]}}}, "control_ids": ["SEC-01", "IAM-01"]}, {"source": {"type": "aws_secretsmanager_secret", "id": "example-db-app"}, "target": {"type": "external_secret", "name": "chat-bravo-demo-db"}, "document": {"apiVersion": "external-secrets.io/v1beta1", "kind": "ExternalSecret", "metadata": {"name": "chat-bravo-demo-db", "namespace": "chat"}, "spec": {"refreshInterval": "1h", "secretStoreRef": {"kind": "ClusterSecretStore", "name": "bravo-platform-openbao"}, "target": {"name": "bravo-demo-db", "creationPolicy": "Owner"}, "data": [{"secretKey": "password", "remoteRef": {"key": "envs/target-onprem/chat-db", "property": "app_writer"}}]}}, "control_ids": ["SEC-01", "ENC-02"]}, {"source": {"type": "aws_iam_role", "id": "chat-app"}, "target": {"type": "k8s_rbac", "name": "chat-bravo-demo-db-reader"}, "document": {"apiVersion": "v1", "kind": "List", "items": [{"apiVersion": "rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1", "kind": "Role", "metadata": {"name": "chat-bravo-demo-db-reader", "namespace": "chat"}, "rules": [{"apiGroups": [""], "resources": ["secrets"], "resourceNames": ["bravo-demo-db"], "verbs": ["get"]}]}, {"apiVersion": "rbac.authorization.k8s.io/v1", "kind": "RoleBinding", "metadata": {"name": "chat-bravo-demo-db-reader", "namespace": "chat"}, "roleRef": {"apiGroup": "rbac.authorization.k8s.io", "kind": "Role", "name": "chat-bravo-demo-db-reader"}, "subjects": [{"kind": "ServiceAccount", "name": "chat-bravo-demo", "namespace": "chat"}]}]}, "control_ids": ["IAM-01", "ISO-01"]}], "exception_justifications": [{"control_id": "NET-01", "justification": "OBJ-06 (deny plain HTTP) returned 400 InvalidRequest in attempts 1 and 2. This looks like a rejection at the RGW or endpoint layer before the bucket policy is evaluated, not a policy decision. The proposed policy has an explicit Deny on aws:SecureTransport=false for all principals and all app actions. If the endpoint rejects plain HTTP outright, the transport requirement is still enforced, just one layer earlier than the probe expects. A human approver should confirm whether the RGW endpoint is TLS-only, and whether a 400 at the transport layer counts as compliant for NET-01, or whether the probe or endpoint configuration needs to change. This proposal does not decide that."}], "audit_summary": "Translations proposed (no verdict made, no controls marked as passed):\n1) rgw_bucket_policy chat-attachments-policy for bucket bravo-demo-attachments: allows the app principal (OBC user) Get/Put/Delete on objects and List on the bucket. A Deny for all principals blocks every listed action when aws:SecureTransport=false. Anonymous access and other credentials have no allow, so they are denied by default. Controls: IAM-01, NET-01, ENC-01, AUD-01.\n2) openbao_policy app-target-onprem-chat-bravo-demo: read only on secret/data/envs/target-onprem/chat-db. Controls: SEC-01, IAM-01.\n3) external_secret chat-bravo-demo-db in namespace chat: ClusterSecretStore bravo-platform-openbao, key envs/target-onprem/chat-db, property app_writer, written to Secret bravo-demo-db key password. Replaces the in-app Secrets Manager SDK call. Controls: SEC-01, ENC-02.\n4) k8s_rbac chat-bravo-demo-db-reader: namespaced Role and RoleBinding in chat, get on secrets/bravo-demo-db only, for SA chat-bravo-demo. Controls: IAM-01, ISO-01.\nOpen issue: OBJ-06 failed twice with 400 InvalidRequest (inconclusive) on the plain-HTTP probe, and the cause is outside what the policy can show. Risk is high, and a NET-01 exception is drafted for the human approver. Unresolved: the gate was unreachable for control details, and the earlier attempts' policies were not available to compare."}, "artifact_digest": "sha256:9cae33a5ec27ddccdc0d6e04298108278b94a49ae178e56c45830889e37081fb", "verifier": {"run_id": "verify-778b074a-gov-3/verify-runner-t-9da3b69b45", "pod_uid": "ff8f3a48-1bea-48a2-942e-a9a7be208097", "image_digest": "sha256:6dd8b6dab6b3adc7812bab69eca5dbdc1a5cc690ad28306d234ffb4ef8ac9753", "image_id": "docker.io/library/import-2026-11-02@sha256:269d3589b15452e1f3188a0c67cc944084c458bdd98faf7c58787a82a42add39", "task_version": "4d55c82b77fcba3b2a9ad1bfe706e461aff3857379f30359a6bb6f6f6304bc12", "artifact_digest": "sha256:9cae33a5ec27ddccdc0d6e04298108278b94a49ae178e56c45830889e37081fb", "reward": 1.0, "checks": [{"name": "behavioral:policy_applied", "ok": true, "detail": "204"}, {"name": "behavioral:gate_OBJ-01", "ok": true, "detail": "PASS anonymous_read_denied 403 AccessDenied"}, {"name": "behavioral:gate_OBJ-02", "ok": true, "detail": "PASS anonymous_list_denied 403 AccessDenied"}, {"name": "behavioral:gate_OBJ-03", "ok": true, "detail": "PASS anonymous_write_denied 403 AccessDenied"}, {"name": "behavioral:gate_OBJ-04", "ok": true, "detail": "PASS app_read_write_allowed ok 200"}, {"name": "behavioral:gate_OBJ-05", "ok": true, "detail": "PASS other_credential_denied 403 AccessDenied"}, {"name": "behavioral:gate_OBJ-06", "ok": false, "detail": "UNKNOWN plain_http_inconclusive error 400 InvalidRequest"}], "refused_uploads": ["/logs/artifacts"], "verifier_kind": "behavioral:gate_obj01_06+static_rules", "collected_at": "2026-11-02T18:24:52.428336+00:00", "behavioral": {"ran": true, "reason": null, "namespace": "verify-778b074a-gov-3-job", "test_bucket": "bravo-rehearsal-verify", "kind": "behavioral:gate_obj01_06+static_rules", "pinned_image": "721622471953.dkr.ecr.ap-northeast-2.amazonaws.com/bravo-platform/gate@sha256:ec47f7c35ef9d83f0a5ef2bdf16b0be2e9c1e9eef813647c2db3c3f864aa5959", "pinned_image_digest": "sha256:ec47f7c35ef9d83f0a5ef2bdf16b0be2e9c1e9eef813647c2db3c3f864aa5959"